Saphira geomyidae -- operator guide
===================================

Your live Gopher content is stored in:

    /srv/gopher

Main menu:

    /srv/gopher/gophermap

Edit it with:

    vi /srv/gopher/gophermap

Add normal text files anywhere under:

    /srv/gopher/

Files under /usr/share/geomyidae/default/ are package-owned
templates and reference copies only.  They are never read by the
running server and are only used to seed /srv/gopher on first
start.  Do not edit them -- edit /srv/gopher instead.  Upgrades may
refresh the templates but never touch your live content.

Example gophermap entries
-------------------------

    iWelcome to my Gopher server
    0About this server    /about.txt    example.com    70
    1Documents            /docs         example.com    70
    9Download file        /files/file.tar.gz example.com 70
    hWebsite              URL:https://example.com

Item types:

    i = informational text (not selectable)
    0 = text file
    1 = directory/menu
    9 = binary/download
    h = URL/HTML link

Important: fields are TAB-separated where required.  The selector,
host and port fields after the description are separated by literal
TAB characters, not spaces.

On a geomyidae server you can leave the host and port fields EMPTY
(just keep the TABs) and the server fills in its own address
automatically -- this is usually what you want:

    0About this server	/about.txt		

    (description, TAB, selector, TAB, TAB -- host and port empty)

Geomyidae specifics
-------------------

- Directory menus can also be written as index.gph files inside the
  directory itself; /srv/gopher/gophermap is simply the root menu.
- A directory without a gophermap/index.gph gets an automatic file
  listing generated by the server.
- The server runs as the unprivileged `gopher` account (UID 123) and
  listens on TCP/70 for both IPv4 and IPv6.
- Service control:
      OpenRC:  rc-service geomyidae start | stop | status
      systemd: systemctl start geomyidae | stop | status
- Neither init system enables the service automatically; enable it
  explicitly with `rc-update add geomyidae` or
  `systemctl enable --now geomyidae`.
